      "impact_policy": {
        "local_depth": 3,
        "boundary_mode": "contract-only",
        "contract_depth": 1,
        "requirement_depth": 1
      },
      "criteria": [
        "A blocker-only producer summary over canonical high, major, and blocker findings is normalized once before collection with before/after, derivation authority, and proven equivalence; findings stay byte-identical, collection completes when otherwise valid, and no producer rewrite is requested.",
        "A substantive result mutation cannot be normalized: only its affected slot is reissued within the attempt bound, unchanged siblings remain sealed, and the new attempt retains original run and slot lineage.",
        "Wrong-producer, copied, sibling-worktree, stale-lease, wrong-run, missing-slot, duplicate-slot, and engine-mismatch fixtures remain non-approvable; only exact once-complete slot and acceptance-evidence conservation permits approval.",
        "Dashboard, status, and inline projection render for coding, read-only, ReviewKernel, released, and legacy contracts and show available scope/write allowance; no missing coding object raises KeyError.",
        "CLI and dashboard parse and ReviewKernel start smoke tests pass on supported Python 3.10, 3.11, and 3.12; an unsupported interpreter fails before state creation with one actionable version error.",
        "While a ReviewKernel run is active and collection is incomplete, repository status resolves the same run id and manifest that review collect can operate on.",
        "Validation needs-user payloads, Product/Engineering guidance, and CLI docs expose the same executable dynamic, render, and static continuation and identify the canonical inline dashboard artifact.",
        "Regression fixtures retain PR-commit and README DoR derivation, explicit dynamic-validation consent receipt, out-of-scope write denial, immutable provenance/findings, early truthful request-changes, and approval conservation.",
        "A bound evaluator outage remains unavailable rather than pass or fail, keeps readiness closed, retries evaluation without opening a product-fix cycle, and reuses cache only on the exact evaluator, engine, capability, repository, worktree, and validity key.",
        "Parallel DoD and evaluator evidence bind to the exact claimed task worktree whether invoked from primary or worker checkout; parent, sibling, moved, dirty, and stale trees cannot substitute."
      ],
      "model": "standard"
    },
